<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Esteve Irmaos to wind down soybean trading.</title>
<headline>Brazil Esteve Irmaos to wind down soybean trading.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil trade house Esteve Irmaos is to cease trading in soybeans and concentrate on its traditional commodity operations in coffee and cotton, one of the company's directors said.</p>
<p>&quot;All our contracts that are still open will be met....But then we will give greater emphasis on our traditional commodity operations in coffee and cotton,&quot; said Antonio Esteve.</p>
<p>The company has been involved in the soybean market for the past 18 years but in the last few years, volumes have been only 50,000 to 80,000 tonnes annually, he added.</p>
<p>-- Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
